Generated datasets — no redistribution
======================================

Copyright 2026 Buy Risk (https://buyrisk.org)

The files in this directory are NOT covered by the repository's software
licence (../../../LICENSE) or its content licence (../../../CONTENT-LICENSE.md),
and no licence to redistribute them is granted.

Why
---

These are derived aggregates, computed by the reducers in /scripts from
third-party datasets. Several of those datasets are held under licences that
permit publishing derived summary statistics but do NOT permit sublicensing
the results to anyone else. Buy Risk can publish these aggregates on its own
site; Buy Risk cannot grant you the right to republish them, because Buy Risk
does not hold that right to give.

Affected in particular are everything derived from the licensed CRSP pull
(fund survivorship, loads and 12b-1 fees, the behaviour gap, index
concentration, diversification, superstocks) and from the licensed
Thomson/Refinitiv s12 holdings pull (fund overlap), plus the Petajisto
active-share panels. Aggregates from public sources (Damodaran, French,
Shiller, SSA, IRS, FRED) carry their own providers' terms, which are generally
permissive but are still the providers' to set, not ours.

What you can do
---------------

- READ these files, and read the reducer that produced each one. That is the
  point of publishing them: the arithmetic behind every figure on the site is
  auditable, and each file's header names the reducer and the command that
  regenerates it.
- REPRODUCE them yourself. If you hold your own licence to the underlying
  data, run the reducers against it and check that our numbers match. That is
  the strongest form of verification available and it is welcome.
- CITE the original sources, which every page and every file header names.

What you cannot do
------------------

- Redistribute these files, or the numbers in them as a dataset, whether
  standalone, inside a fork, or inside any other product.

A fork of this repository must delete this directory, and regenerate it from
data the fork is itself licensed to use.

Questions: buyriskHQ@gmail.com
